---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---

<PageLayout 
	title="DiceForce IT | Cookie Policy" 
	description="Cookie Policy for DiceForce IT. Understand how we use cookies and tracking technologies to improve your experience and manage your preferences."
	activePage="none"
>
	<div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto w-full flex flex-col gap-12 pt-10 pb-20">
		<!-- Page Header -->
		<section class="space-y-4 animate-stagger-item">
			<div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 border border-white/5 rounded-full bg-white/[0.01]">
				<span class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-cyan-400/80 uppercase">Cookie & Tracking Governance</span>
			</div>
			<h1 class="font-syne font-black text-4xl sm:text-5xl md:text-6xl tracking-tighter leading-none text-white select-text">
				Cookie Policy
			</h1>
			<p class="text-neutral-500 font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest">
				Effective Date: August 3, 2026
			</p>
		</section>

		<!-- Content Blocks -->
		<section class="border-t border-white/5 pt-12 space-y-12 animate-stagger-item font-light leading-relaxed text-neutral-300">
			<!-- Preamble -->
			<div class="space-y-4">
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					<strong class="text-white font-medium">DiceForce IT</strong> ("DiceForce IT", "we", "our", or "us") uses cookies, tracking pixels, and similar web technologies to enhance your browsing experience, analyze site performance, ensure security, and optimize our digital services.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					This Cookie Policy explains what cookies are, how we use them, the categories of cookies deployed on our website, and how you can control or adjust your cookie preferences.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					This policy should be read alongside our <a href="/privacy" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/terms" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">Terms of Service</a>.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Section 1: What Are Cookies -->
			<div class="space-y-4 border-t border-white/5 pt-8">
				<h2 class="font-syne font-semibold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white tracking-tight">
					1. What Are Cookies?
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					Cookies are small text files that are stored on your device (computer, tablet, or mobile phone) when you visit a website. They allow the website to recognize your device, remember user preferences, maintain session security, and provide statistical insights into website usage.
				</p>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					Cookies may be "session cookies" (which are deleted automatically when you close your browser) or "persistent cookies" (which remain stored on your device until they expire or are manually deleted).
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Section 2: Categories of Cookies We Use -->
			<div class="space-y-6 border-t border-white/5 pt-8">
				<h2 class="font-syne font-semibold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white tracking-tight">
					2. Categories of Cookies We Use
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					We categorize the cookies and web technologies used on our platform as follows:
				</p>

				<!-- Essential Cookies -->
				<div class="space-y-3 pl-2 sm:pl-4 border-l-2 border-cyan-500/30">
					<h3 class="font-syne font-medium text-lg text-white">A. Strictly Necessary / Essential Cookies</h3>
					<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
						These cookies are indispensable for the website to function properly. They enable core functionalities such as page navigation, secure authentication, network security, and accessibility. You cannot disable essential cookies through our site, as the website cannot operate properly without them.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Performance & Analytics Cookies -->
				<div class="space-y-3 pl-2 sm:pl-4 border-l-2 border-cyan-500/30">
					<h3 class="font-syne font-medium text-lg text-white">B. Performance & Analytics Cookies</h3>
					<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
						Performance cookies collect aggregated information about how visitors use our website—such as which pages are visited most frequently, site loading speeds, and any error messages encountered. These insights help us optimize site layout, user workflows, and technical stability.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Functional Cookies -->
				<div class="space-y-3 pl-2 sm:pl-4 border-l-2 border-cyan-500/30">
					<h3 class="font-syne font-medium text-lg text-white">C. Functionality Cookies</h3>
					<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
						Functionality cookies enable our site to remember choices you make (such as language preferences or region selection) and provide enhanced, personalized features.
					</p>
				</div>

				<!-- Targeting / Marketing Cookies -->
				<div class="space-y-3 pl-2 sm:pl-4 border-l-2 border-cyan-500/30">
					<h3 class="font-syne font-medium text-lg text-white">D. Marketing & Communication Cookies</h3>
					<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
						These cookies may be set through our site by our analytics and marketing partners to build a profile of your interests and show you relevant content or recruitment opportunities across other digital properties.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- Section 3: Third-Party Services -->
			<div class="space-y-4 border-t border-white/5 pt-8">
				<h2 class="font-syne font-semibold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white tracking-tight">
					3. Third-Party Web Technologies & Analytics
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					In addition to our first-party technologies, third-party service providers (such as web hosting providers, analytics services, and social media platforms) may deploy cookies when you interact with embedded components or external links on our site. Third-party cookies are governed by the respective privacy policies of those third-party providers.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Section 4: How to Manage Cookie Preferences -->
			<div class="space-y-4 border-t border-white/5 pt-8">
				<h2 class="font-syne font-semibold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white tracking-tight">
					4. Managing & Disabling Cookie Preferences
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					You have full control over your cookie settings. You can manage, block, or delete cookies at any time through your web browser settings. Most modern browsers allow you to:
				</p>
				<ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-sm text-neutral-300">
					<li>View stored cookies and delete them individually or en masse</li>
					<li>Block third-party cookies</li>
					<li>Block cookies from specific websites</li>
					<li>Prevent all cookies from being stored</li>
					<li>Clear all cookies when you close your browser</li>
				</ul>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base pt-2">
					Please note that if you choose to restrict or block essential cookies, certain features or interactive sections of our website may not function as intended.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Section 5: Updates to Cookie Policy -->
			<div class="space-y-4 border-t border-white/5 pt-8">
				<h2 class="font-syne font-semibold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white tracking-tight">
					5. Updates to This Cookie Policy
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					We may update this Cookie Policy from time to time to reflect technological changes, regulatory requirements, or updates to our operational practices. Any changes will be published on this page with an updated effective date.
				</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Section 6: Contact Us -->
			<div class="space-y-4 border-t border-white/5 pt-8">
				<h2 class="font-syne font-semibold text-xl sm:text-2xl text-white tracking-tight">
					6. Contact Us
				</h2>
				<p class="text-sm sm:text-base">
					If you have any questions or concerns regarding our Cookie Policy or data management practices, please contact us:
				</p>
				<div class="text-sm sm:text-base bg-white/[0.01] border border-white/5 p-4 rounded-xl space-y-1 font-mono text-neutral-300">
					<p class="font-semibold text-white">DiceForce IT</p>
					<p>Texas, United States</p>
					<p>Email: <a href="mailto:hr@diceforceit.com" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">hr@diceforceit.com</a></p>
					<p>Phone: <a href="tel:+14694605006" class="text-neutral-300 hover:text-white transition-colors">+1 469-460-5006</a></p>
				</div>
			</div>

			<!-- CTA / Back button -->
			<div class="pt-8 border-t border-white/5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6">
				<p class="text-neutral-500 text-xs">
					Have questions about data privacy? Contact <a href="mailto:hr@diceforceit.com" class="text-cyan-400 hover:underline">hr@diceforceit.com</a>.
				</p>
				
				<div class="relative group transition-transform duration-500 hover:scale-[1.015]">
					<div class="absolute -inset-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-[#0377ff] via-[#00deff] to-[#883ae2] rounded-full blur-md opacity-25 group-hover:opacity-60 transition-all duration-500 ease-out"></div>
					<div class="relative rounded-full p-[1px] overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center bg-black">
						<div class="absolute inset-[-200%] bg-[conic-gradient(from_0deg,#0377ff,#00deff,#883ae2,#00deff,#0377ff)] animate-border-spin"></div>
						<a 
							href="/" 
							class="relative px-8 py-3 bg-black hover:bg-neutral-900 text-white font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest rounded-full transition-all duration-300 inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-2 cursor-pointer z-10 select-none group-hover:text-[#00deff]"
						>
							Back to Experience
						</a>
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
